          "worked_solution": "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & -{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 & {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} & 0 \\\\ -2{x}_{3} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3} & -{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+\\frac{2}{13}{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are  the $1$st,  $2$nd and $3$rd. Therefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{13}{2}{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nConsequently, ${A,B,C}$ is linearly independent.",
